Cross-compile fix: do not RUN the (arm64) extract-strings host tool.

src/xml/extract-strings is compiled with the cross compiler (aarch64) but the
Makefile then EXECUTES it on the build host to regenerate src/xml/xmli18n-tmp.h
(an i18n/NLS translation-string header). On a cross build the freshly-built
aarch64 binary cannot run on the x86_64 macOS host:
    ./extract-strings: cannot execute binary file

The tarball already SHIPS a pre-generated src/xml/xmli18n-tmp.h (6908 lines),
and that header is consumed only by po/*.po (NLS) at *dist* time -- nothing in a
--disable-nls build #includes it. So the regeneration step is unnecessary here.

This patch (against src/xml/Makefile.in so it survives ./configure):
  1. Drops xmli18n-tmp.h from CLEANFILES so the shipped copy is NOT deleted.
  2. Replaces the regeneration recipe with a cross-safe no-op: keep the shipped
     header; if missing, create an empty placeholder (harmless for --disable-nls).
     extract-strings is no longer a prerequisite, so it is never RUN (it is still
     compiled as a noinst_PROGRAM -- a harmless aarch64 link, never executed).

build-gutenprint.sh additionally restores the pristine xmli18n-tmp.h from the
tarball before (re)building, in case a previous failed run already removed it.

--- a/src/xml/Makefile.in
+++ b/src/xml/Makefile.in
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@
 extract_strings_SOURCES = extract-strings.c
 extract_strings_LDADD = $(GUTENPRINT_LIBS)
 # xmli18n-tmp.h is needed by po/POTFILES.in at dist time
-CLEANFILES = xmli18n-tmp.h xmli18n-tmp.h.tmp xml-stamp xml-stamp.tmp
+CLEANFILES = xmli18n-tmp.h.tmp xml-stamp xml-stamp.tmp
 EXTRA_DIST = $(pkgxmldata_DATA) xmli18n-tmp.h
 MAINTAINERCLEANFILES = Makefile.in
 all: all-recursive
@@ -880,10 +880,10 @@

 all-local: xmli18n-tmp.h xml-stamp

-xmli18n-tmp.h: xml-stamp extract-strings
-	-rm -f $@ $@.tmp
-	./extract-strings `cat xml-stamp | sed -e 's;^;$(srcdir)/;'` > $@.tmp
-	mv $@.tmp $@
+xmli18n-tmp.h: xml-stamp
+	@if test ! -f $(srcdir)/xmli18n-tmp.h && test ! -f xmli18n-tmp.h; then \
+	  echo "/* cross build: NLS string table intentionally empty */" > xmli18n-tmp.h; \
+	fi

 dist-hook: xmli18n-tmp.h xml-stamp
